  <p class="subjects-source-note">Course names and codes follow the Ontario Ministry of Education secondary mathematics curriculum and Lambton College's published course list. Ministries and colleges update codes and offerings periodically, so it's worth confirming current details against a student's actual course outline before booking.</p>
</section>

<section id="about">
  <h2>About Preeti</h2>
  <p class="section-lede">Ontario College of Teachers certified (Junior Division; Intermediate Mathematics &amp; Science; Senior Division Mathematics), with an M.Sc. in Mathematics from Himachal Pradesh University.</p>
  <p>Teaching experience began in India, from 2008 to 2018, across secondary-level classrooms, followed by four years of tutoring and teaching experience in Ontario — including LTO and occasional teaching positions with the Lambton Kent, Superior-Greenstone, and Superior North school boards, and a stint as a subject tutor at Mathnasium. Comfortable across the full range of the curriculum, from a Grade 8 student catching up on fractions to a college student working through Calc II or business statistics.</p>
  <p>Sessions run one-to-one or in small batches with other students on the same subject, so instruction stays targeted to where each student actually needs help. Tutoring is in person by default; online sessions are available on special request.</p>
  <ul class="skills-list">
    <li>Curriculum-aligned instruction across Ontario Grade 8–12 math and Lambton College courses</li>
    <li>Diagnostic approach that pinpoints and closes specific gaps rather than re-teaching everything</li>
    <li>Clear, step-by-step explanations paced to how each student learns</li>
    <li>Experience supporting English Language Learners (ESL)</li>
    <li>Multilingual support in English, Hindi, and Punjabi</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="how">
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <div class="steps">
    <div class="step">
      <div class="num"></div>
      <div>
        <h3>Free 20-minute intro call</h3>
        <p>We talk through what's going on in the class, what's been tried already, and whether we're a good fit before anything is booked.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="step">
      <div class="num"></div>
      <div>
        <h3>A short baseline check</h3>
        <p>A handful of problems, not a test, to see exactly which skills are solid and which ones are shaky — so the first real session isn't spent guessing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="step">
      <div class="num"></div>
      <div>
        <h3>Hourly sessions, on a schedule that fits</h3>
        <p>Sessions are booked by the hour and can run weekly, biweekly, or a few times a week when there's a syllabus to cover before a test or exam. In person by default; online available on special request.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="step">
      <div class="num"></div>
      <div>
        <h3>Notes after every session</h3>
        <p>A short recap of what we covered and what to practice before next time, sent the same day.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

